sherpa-onnx-tts (2.0.1+deps2-6) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Rename to sherpa-onnx-tts and move out of the public paths, so that a
    distribution sherpa-onnx can be installed beside it: the libraries in
    the new libsherpa-onnx-tts in /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts (beside the
    private onnxruntime), headers in /usr/include/linux-tts with
    libsherpa-onnx-tts-dev, the tools in /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts/
    sherpa-onnx/bin with the new package sherpa-say (/usr/bin/sherpa-say).
    The C API has no stable ABI: the modules depend on the exact version.

 -- Grigory Tuboltsev <gtubolcev@gmail.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 03:00:00 +0100

sherpa-onnx (2.0.1+deps2-5) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Build against the private onnxruntime 1.32 of libonnxruntime-tts
    (RUNPATH /usr/lib/<triplet>/linux-tts) instead of the distribution's.
  * Add the "vulkan" provider, which loads the onnx-vulkan-rs plugin EP.
  * -2 to -4 were local test builds.

 -- Grigory Tuboltsev <gtubolcev@gmail.com>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0100

